+## When beforeSession throws
+
+- `beforeSession` is awaited inside the orchestrator's `try` block, so a thrown `Error` fires `onError(session, error)` and `afterSession(session)` before the rejection propagates unchanged to the caller ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- A throw from `beforeSession` aborts the turn before `beforeUserInput`, `afterUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, any provider or tool call, and `afterModelResponse`, while still running `onError`, `afterSession` and `sessionStore.save` in order; `afterSession` runs unconditionally with `(session)` because a multi-step `beforeSession` may fail after acquiring an earlier resource, so an `afterSession` hook cannot assume `beforeSession` completed and must guard its own teardown when releasing state that might never have been allocated ([validated by: aborts the turn before input or provider steps and still runs onError, afterSession and save](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.test.ts#L10)).
